    "rich_text_DiY63V": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_TfKazJ": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The Gold Standard of Hygiene: Our 100% Filtration Guarantee"
          }
        },
        "text_Unqhjy": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p><a href=\"https://floathub.co.uk/\"><strong>Float Hub</strong></a><strong> is the only London centre with a 100% filtration guarantee between every single guest. </strong>Most pods, while offering a sterile environment with hydrogen peroxide & high salt levels, only employ a surface skimmer to remove detritus.</p><p>Our state-of-the-art technology ensures that 100% of the water volume is filtered <strong>three times</strong> before your session begins.</p><ol><li><strong>Oversized Pod Design:</strong> We don’t do cramped spaces. Every single one of our custom pods is explicitly engineered to be oversized, entirely eliminating the claustrophobic feel of traditional tanks to give your body true room to drift.</li><li><strong>Industrial-Grade Micron Filtration:</strong> We trap particles as small as 1 micron (standard pool filters often miss anything under 20 microns).</li><li><strong>High-Intensity UV Sterilisation:</strong> Every drop of water passes through powerful Ultraviolet light, neutralizing 99.9% of bacteria and viruses. This UV light reacts with the safe levels of hydrogen peroxide we maintain, meaning the combined sanitising effect is many times stronger than systems without both.</li><li><strong>Natural Mineral Sterility:</strong> The 30% Epsom salt concentration is naturally hostile to pathogens, but we supplement this with automated pH and disinfectant monitoring to ensure laboratory-grade water purity.</li><li><strong>White Light Standard: </strong>We are the only large centre in London that chooses white light either side of sessions, because we are entirely confident in the clarity and extreme cleanliness of our solution. Some other centres use low blue lighting in their pods, making it harder to see impurities and impossible to detect discolouration—either by customers or their own staff performing quality checks.</li></ol>"
          }
        }
      },
