    "rich_text_nTbELB": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_tjhk3t": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "The “Theta State”: Why Your Brain Needs a “Dark Mode”"
          }
        },
        "text_zQiLtx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>During a typical 60-minute session, your brain waves transition from active Beta waves to relaxed Alpha waves, eventually settling into the <strong>Theta state</strong>. This is the elusive “twilight” zone usually only accessible during deep REM sleep or years of meditative practice.</p><p>In the Theta state, the two hemispheres of your brain communicate more effectively. This leads to:</p><ul><li><strong>Enhanced Problem Solving:</strong> Many London professionals use the tank to “work through” complex business challenges.</li><li><strong>Emotional Regulation:</strong> A profound sense of detachment that allows you to process stress without the typical physical “fight or flight” response.</li><li><strong>The “Afterglow”:</strong> The mental clarity and calm you feel doesn’t end when you leave the tank; the “Post-Float Afterglow” typically lasts for 24–48 hours.</li></ul>"
          }
        }
      },
