    "rich_text_jtrkYk": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_TE7C6X": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Floating vs. Meditation: Why the Tank is Faster"
          }
        },
        "text_cVkPnW": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Traditional meditation is difficult because of physical distractions: a sore back, a noisy street, or the itch you can’t scratch. Sensory deprivation is “meditation on training wheels.” By removing the body’s input to the brain, your mind has no choice but to settle. It is the fastest route to a meditative state available in the modern world.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
